  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">220000027 ICMP support for Iraq to build a sustainable process for accounting for missing persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of this project is to assist Iraq in implementing a sustainable strategy to account for all missing persons and to secure the rights of families of the missing. This multi-year strategy will center on the conclusions of an ICMP-hosted high-level policy conference in The Hague in 2021. During this conference, broad consensus was reached on 12 conclusions forming the basis for a comprehensive strategy. These conclusions included, among others, creating a central mechanism and adopting a national plan, improving data management and data protection, ensuring state funding for the process, strengthening the role and capacity of civil society, upholding the rights of survivors, particularly women, and bringing perpetrators to justice.</narrative>
  </description>
